<%# "Read" is when the passage was taken from the source, and it is here because
    of what happened on 2026-09-22: two readings of a web page, taken on the
    20th, were counted as contradicting a claim about what that page said on the
    8th — the page having been revised on the 10th. The scorer did as the links
    told it; nothing on the page let a reader see that the contradiction was
    younger than the thing it contradicted (Stage 41).

    It is display only. Nothing here reaches scoring, and a date beside a link
    decides nothing; it lets a reader ask the question. %>
<%# A card per link rather than a row of seven columns: the statement and the
    note are prose, and a table gave each a column a word wide on a phone and a
    sliver beside the outline on a desktop (2026-09-23). %>
<% if links.any? %>
  <ul class="rows">
  <% links.each do |l| %>
    <% read_at = l.dig(:evidence, :source, :retrieved_at) %>
    <li class="<%= 'muted-row' unless l[:counted] %>">
      <div class="lead"><%= link_to l[:evidence][:statement] || "[withheld]", evidence_path(l[:evidence_item_id]) %></div>
      <p class="facts">
        <span>From <%= link_to l[:evidence][:source][:title] || "[withheld]", source_path(l[:evidence][:source][:id]) %></span>
        <span title="When this passage was taken from the source. A reading later than the thing a claim is about may be a different version of it.">Read <b><%= read_at ? read_at.to_date.iso8601 : "—" %></b></span>
        <span>Relevance <b><%= l[:relevance_strength] %></b></span>
        <span>Steps <b><%= l[:interpretive_steps] %></b></span>
        <span><b><%= l[:counted] ? "Counted" : "Not counted" %></b></span>
      </p>
      <% if l[:note].present? %><p class="aside"><%= l[:note] %></p><% end %>
    </li>
  <% end %>
  </ul>
<% else %><p class="muted">None.</p><% end %>
